WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.160
This new image from NASA's James Webb&nbsp;
Space Telescope shows about 50 young stars,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:13.440
many of them similar in mass to our sun. They&nbsp;
are in the Rho Ophiuchi cloud complex. What&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:18.480
we're seeing here is essentially a stellar&nbsp;
nursery. A place where baby stars are being&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:23.220
born. Those beautiful red jets that you see&nbsp;
there in the image are the telltale signs&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:29.160
of these baby stars bursting forth from their&nbsp;
cosmic cocoons and the dust that you see here&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:35.340
is really reminiscent of how our own sun&nbsp;
was born billions of years ago and all the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:39.720
dust similar to what you see here eventually of&nbsp;
course formed the planets including the Earth.

